DiamondHead Beach Resort, through its agent, The Neighborhood Company, requests approval of a Commercial Planned Development (CPD) rezoning for approximately 2.38 acres at 1999 and 2000 Estero Boulevard within the Times Square Mixed-Use/Pedestrian Commercial designations on the Future Land Use map. The request would recognize the existing resort, incorporate the existing parking parcel north of Estero Boulevard, and allow redevelopment and expansion of the existing resort.
The DiamondHead Beach Resort was originally approved by Lee County through Development Order (DO) No. 94-12-024, prior to the incorporation of the Town of Fort Myers Beach. According to the applicant, the original Development Order approved 154 resort units in two phases. Phase I, consisting of approximately 124 resort units and associated amenities, was constructed. Phase II authorized 30 additional resort units and a parking structure. In 2018, three hotel units were removed to accommodate construction of the Coste Island Cuisine restaurant. Staff understand that 121 hotel rooms currently exist while the construction of the restaurant accounted for the 3 unbuilt units from first phase. Thus, according to the applicant, 30 previously approved hotel units remain unbuilt.
The CPD application proposes 55 additional hotel rooms consisting of 30 unbuilt rooms and 25 additional rooms beyond the vested entitlement, resulting in a maximum of 176 hotel rooms. The applicant submitted supporting documentation including correspondence, project process sheets, and prior approval records indicating approval of the original Development Order and subsequent amendments. The application also incorporates the existing parking parcel located at 1999 Estero Boulevard, which has historically operated under Special Exception Resolution 03-11 for employees and overflow guest parking. The applicant acknowledges that approval of the proposed CPD would supersede and vacate the existing Special Exception.
No amendment to the Future Land Use category has been submitted with this application.
Proposed Development
The revised Master Concept Plan proposes:
Expansion of the existing resort from 121 existing hotel rooms to a maximum of 176 hotel rooms;
Recognition of the previously approved 30 unbuilt hotel units together with 25 additional rooms;
Existing restaurant and outdoor seating areas totaling approximately 8,295 square feet: Cabanas Beach Bar & Grill, 1,870 square feet under the building plus 1,600 square feet of outdoor seating; and Coste Island Cuisine, 4,825 square feet;
A new detached three-story amenity/event building, including parking/access below, covered viewing/gathering space, approximately 2,750 gross square feet of enclosed event space, and rooftop viewing access; no guest rooms are identified in this building;
Improvements to the existing parking facilities on both the primary resort parcel and the parking parcel north of Estero Boulevard;
Continued use of existing access points from Estero Boulevard with no new vehicular access proposed; and
Pedestrian connections between the north parking parcel and the main resort property.
On September 8th, 2006, the LPA unanimously (6-0) recommended denial of CPD 20260099 as presented. The recommendation was based primarily on the proposed 24-unit beachside building and the insufficiency of the identified public benefits to justify its requested height, intensity, and compatibility impacts. The LPA generally supported the 33-unit addition to the existing resort building but did not support the scale and location of the separate beachside building.
On October 5th, 2026, the town council voted 2-1 for LPA rehearing of the CPD 20260099 with all the changes provided to the council after the LPA meeting.
